WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
A new chat. The same work, ready to continue.

2
00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:09.300
Start with fictional notes for a website proposal.

3
00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:13.300
Save the source material and first draft as a Retulo task.

4
00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:19.100
The first version is saved as proposal-v001.md.

5
00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:22.900
The task ID connects the sources, output and saved progress.

6
00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:26.500
In a new Codex chat, ask for a three-week schedule
and keep the first version.

7
00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:32.900
We replay the actual Retulo command on the same demo task.
The output identifies the original file.

8
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:37.400
The original file becomes the starting point for the revision.

9
00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:44.050
Only the schedule changes. The page scope and constraints stay the same.

10
00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:49.250
The first version has the same SHA-256 before and after.

11
00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:54.000
Version 1 stays intact. Version 2 is saved as a separate file.

12
00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Keep the files. Continue the work. Retulo.
